},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000162585","entrez_id":["199990"],"uniprot":["Q6NZ36"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables K63-linked polyubiquitin modification-dependent protein binding activity and ubiquitin-dependent protein binding activity. Involved in interstrand cross-link repair and translesion synthesis. Located in cell junction; chromosome; and nuclear body. Part of Fanconi anaemia nuclear complex. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6NZ36","text":"Component of the Fanconi anemia (FA) complex required to recruit the FA complex to DNA interstrand cross-links (ICLs) and promote ICLs repair. Following DNA damage recognizes and binds 'Lys-63'-linked ubiquitin generated by RNF8 at ICLs and recruits other components of the FA complex. Promotes translesion synthesis via interaction with REV1."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}